//? Title: Random network distillation for grid exploration
//? Lang: en

> Random network distillation for grid exploration

Random network distillation (RND) assigns a novelty bonus to the
successor state. A fixed random network embeds its one-hot state ID.
A separate predictor learns to match that embedding from replay. Half
the squared feature distance acts as the intrinsic reward, so repeated
observations generally earn less reward as prediction improves.

The exploration policy learns from the sum of the task reward and
half the novelty bonus. A second Q-table learns only from task rewards
on the same transitions. The control uses the same schedule with zero
intrinsic reward. The final greedy test uses the task-only table and
starts again in the upper-left cell. Increased coverage and successful
task completion are measured separately.

The plot compares coverage on three matched seeds. The table also
shows predictor error before and after learning on the cells each RND
run actually visited. Seeds reproduce the Datamunge runs. The initial
network weights come from Datamunge's own seeded initializer.

[Burda et al. (2019), Exploration by Random Network Distillation|https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.12894]

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/random_network_distillation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;
  namespace r=dm::rl;
  const auto one_hot=[](const std::vector<int>& ids) {
    return n::one_hot(n::from_vector(ids),49);
  };
  const auto probes=n::eye(49);
  std::vector<double> control,rnd;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::print("| Seed | Mode | Visited | Training goals | Greedy success | Predictor MSE before | Predictor MSE after |\n"
             "|---:|:---|---:|---:|:---|---:|---:|\n");
  for (const auto seed:{43602u,43603u,43604u}) {
    const auto [path,reward,visited,goals,success]=r::sparse_grid_experiment(seed);
    control.push_back(visited);
    std::print("| {} | Control | {} | {} | {} | | |\n",seed,visited,goals,success);
    n::save_npz(std::format("build/{}_control.npz",seed),{{"transitions",path},{"bonus",reward}});

    r::RandomNetworkDistillation model(49,24,12);
    const auto before=model.evaluate(probes);
    const auto [rows,bonus,coverage,hits,solved]=r::sparse_grid_experiment(seed,
        [&](const auto& step) {
          return static_cast<float>(model.evaluate(one_hot({step[2]}))[0].item());
        },
        [&](const auto batch) {
          std::vector<int> ids;
          for (const auto& step:batch) ids.push_back(step[2]);
          model.train(one_hot(ids));
        });
    rnd.push_back(coverage);
    const auto successors=n::slice(rows,{0,2},{rows.size(0),1}).to_vector<int>();
    const auto [error,prediction,target]=model.evaluate(one_hot(successors));
    const auto after=model.evaluate(probes);
    if (before[2].to_vector<float>()!=after[2].to_vector<float>()) {
      throw std::runtime_error("RND target changed during training");
    }
    const std::set<int> unique(successors.begin(),successors.end());
    const auto ids=n::from_vector(std::vector<int>(unique.begin(),unique.end()));
    const double prior=n::mean(n::gather(before[0],ids)).item()/6;
    const double fitted=n::mean(n::gather(after[0],ids)).item()/6;
    std::print("| {} | RND | {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",
               seed,coverage,hits,solved,prior,fitted);
    n::save_npz(std::format("build/{}_rnd.npz",seed),{{"transitions",rows},{"bonus",bonus},
        {"final_error",error},{"prediction",prediction},{"features",target},
        {"probe_target_before",before[2]},{"probe_target_after",after[2]},
        {"probe_prediction_before",before[1]},{"probe_prediction_after",after[1]}});
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.points({43602,43603,43604},control,"Task reward only",{217,96,26},7)
      .points({43602,43603,43604},rnd,"With RND bonus",{37,99,235},7)
      .title("Sparse-grid exploration coverage").x_label("Seed").y_label("Unique cells visited")
      .ylim(0,49).size(820,460).save_svg("build/random_network_distillation.svg");
}
```
